{"module":"Term 1","title":"Unit 5 — Recreation","description":"Leisure activities, the present perfect (ever, never, for, since), invitations.","intro":"This unit is about free time, hobbies, sports and travel.","objectifs":["Talk about leisure activities.","Use the present perfect with ever, never, for, since, just, already, yet.","Invite, accept and refuse."],"cours":[{"t":"Vocabulary","h":"<ul><li>hobbies: hiking, camping, drawing, chess, swimming, surfing the Internet</li><li>go + -ing (go swimming), play + games (play chess), do + activities (do karate)</li></ul>"},{"t":"Grammar: the present perfect","h":"<div class=\"formula key\">have / has + past participle</div><ul><li>Experiences: <i>Have you <b>ever</b> been to Chefchaouen? — No, I’ve <b>never</b> been there.</i></li><li>Duration up to now: <i>I’ve played the guitar <b>for</b> three years / <b>since</b> 2022.</i></li><li>Recent actions: just, already, yet: <i>Have you finished <b>yet</b>?</i></li></ul><div class=\"box note\"><span class=\"box-title\">for / since</span><p><b>for</b> + a period (for two hours) ; <b>since</b> + a starting point (since Monday).</p></div>"},{"t":"Communication: inviting","h":"<ul><li>“Would you like to come to the beach on Sunday?” / “How about going to the cinema?”</li><li>Accept: “I’d love to!” — Refuse: “I’m sorry, I can’t. I have to revise.”</li></ul>"}],"recap":"Present perfect = have / has + past participle (experience, duration, recent action). for + period, since + starting point. Invite: Would you like to…? Accept: I’d love to. Refuse politely: I’m sorry, I can’t…","cards":[["for","+ a period: for 3 years"],["since","+ a starting point: since 2020"],["Have you ever…?","Asks about life experience"],["go / play / do","go swimming, play chess, do karate"]],"exercises":{"facile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"I have lived here ___ 2019.","choices":["since","for","during","ago"],"answer":0,"explain":"2019 is a starting point → since."},{"type":"direct","q":"Past participle of “see”:","accept":["seen"],"display":"seen","explain":"see – saw – seen."},{"type":"qcm","q":"We say: ___ swimming.","choices":["go","play","do","make"],"answer":0,"explain":"Activities ending in -ing usually take “go”."}],"moyen":[{"type":"qcm","q":"Have you ___ eaten couscous with seven vegetables?","choices":["ever","yet","since","already"],"answer":0,"explain":"Life experience question → ever."},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete: She has studied English ___ five years.","accept":["for"],"display":"for","explain":"A period of time → for."},{"type":"qcm","q":"The best polite refusal is:","choices":["I’m sorry, I can’t. I have an exam tomorrow.","No.","I don’t want.","Never!"],"answer":0,"explain":"Apologise and give a reason."}],"difficile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"Choose the correct sentence:","choices":["I have visited Agadir last summer.","I visited Agadir last summer.","I have visit Agadir last summer.","I visiting Agadir last summer."],"answer":1,"explain":"A finished time (last summer) needs the past simple, not the present perfect.","why":["“Last summer” is a finished time: no present perfect.",null,"Wrong form of the participle and wrong tense.","No auxiliary: incorrect."]},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete: “Have you finished your project ___?” (question, end of sentence)","accept":["yet"],"display":"yet","explain":"“Yet” is used in questions and negatives at the end of the sentence."},{"type":"qcm","q":"He has been a member of the club ___ he was ten.","choices":["since","for","ago","during"],"answer":0,"explain":"“He was ten” is a starting point → since."}]}}